                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1561-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Telefunken Elektroakustik M82</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The M82 is a large-diaphragm dynamic microphone, designed primarily for use with kick drums. Two onboard switches provide access to two independent EQ modes, yielding four combinations. </p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/telefunkenusa/M82-switches.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/telefunkenusa/M82-switches-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="M82 Switches" width="220" /></a>The EQ circuits provide:</p><ul><li><b>Kick EQ</b>: a notch around 350Hz, to prevent &#8220;boxiness&#8221; in a kick track.</li><li><b>High Boost</b>: a high shelf to boost frequencies above 2kHz, with a peak of +6dB at 10kHz, to enhance beater click in a drum or articulation on other sources such as vocals or guitar cabinets.</li></ul><p>The mic is a moving-coil dynamic; the EQ circuits are passive circuits. The mic does not require phantom power.</p><p>The capsule is described as &#8220;large diaphragm&#8221; due to its 35mm  diameter.</p><p>The M82 was announced officially at Winter NAMM 2013. It will ship with a zippered storage pouch and a mic clip. A suspension mount will be made available separately.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Telefunken-USA/M82">Telefunken Elektroakustik M82</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2013.</p>
